From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 15:28:45 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 20/20] build05-next r2: day/night toggle inside lakeside
 applies lakeside's own day/night look (fixes the reset to the island light)

Bug: toggling day/night after arriving at the lakeside put the island main light back (WorldFlowComponent.applyDayNight
wrote it and nothing re-applied the lakeside look).
- DayNightContract: onDayNightChange/emitDayNightChange; applyDayNight emits after writing the island light and rig views;
  __worldDayNight.reapply() re-writes the island look for the current mode without locking the override.
- LakesideSceneData: LAKESIDE_NIGHT_LIGHT_PARAMS (moonlight same direction, cool ambient, #1c2740 clear, dark blue fog;
  water main 0.8 / ambient 0.6 / sky 0.12; proxy values) + lakesideModeLighting(mode) (day = unchanged r5h3 dusk).
- LakesideJourneyAtmosphere: targets per mode; island base per mode (day base x island scale, island light colour);
  journey day-base registry; board-holding flag; journey reapply hook.
- New region/LakesideJourneyLighting.ts (moved out of RegionJourneyAdapter): every write uses the current mode; a toggle
  after the blend started re-writes at once, before the blend the island owns the light; while the board shows it stands
  down; restore puts back the capture and, if the mode changed, asks the world to re-write the island look.
- LakesideBoardBackground: applyDir/applyFog per mode incl. board clear colour and water lightParams/fresnel sky strength;
  re-applied on toggle while visible; restore -> journey re-applies (lakeside stop) or the world re-writes (island).
Test: tools/lakeside/test_lakeside_daynight.cjs (suite: lakeside-daynight) - real TS on a fake cc/world: toggle in lakeside
day->night->day, mid-blend toggle, pre-blend toggle stays island, leave in night -> island night, leave then toggle on the
island, board holding/hide; journey-atmosphere test follows the move.
